    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just not just \"grief\" though. it's like the part of me that mattered is gone. i look in the mirror and i don't recognize the person looking back. there is no \"moving forward\" when there's nowhere to go. i've spent my entire adult life being someone else's everything... now i'm nothing. it feels like i'm just waiting for the rest of me to catch up to him.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you, and it's okay to feel as if you're a different person now—that feeling of disconnection is a common part of grief. Opening up to friends, family, or a support group, like GriefShare.org, can be helpful. For now, focusing on small daily tasks, even just sitting in the chair, can sometimes help ground you. You're not alone, even if it feels that way right now. We're here whenever you're ready to speak.",
      "source": "target",
